  "lore": "Hushwing does not land; it condenses. It wades the low fog on legs you can never quite focus on, standing so still that frogs use it for shade. It turns up before you wake, watches the porch for about as long as a kettle takes, then leaves without a sound - but it always tips one wing on the way out. That is as close as weather gets to saying hello.",
